id: pm-prmt1y
title: Isolate published MCP verification from the caller global skill catalog
description: Published-release verification inherits the caller PM roots. A larger global skill catalog paginates bundled pm-sdk out of the first resource page and falsely rejects a healthy published server. Isolate project/global configuration for all npm/npx/bunx stdio and HTTP verification subprocesses without weakening protocol assertions.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-18T15:37:46.481Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-18T16:58:44.833Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-18T15:53:11.453Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-18T15:53:11.453Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Every package verifier subprocess has isolated PM roots; existing MCP discovery checks remain strict; real published npm/npx/bunx stdio and HTTP checks pass.
parent: pm-z3ez
resolution: Isolated PM project/global roots across npm/npx/bunx verification subprocesses and disabled acceptance telemetry/Sentry
expected_result: Healthy published CLI and MCP artifacts pass strict stdio and HTTP acceptance regardless of caller skill catalog
actual_result: Both missing-isolation negative regressions reproduced before fix; 40 verifier cases and linked test pass; real 2026.9.18 npm/npx/bunx stdio/HTTP and missing-binary controls pass
